Basic system information:

set command to check the path from command line

ver : windows version

systeminfo : displays system info

help -  Provides help information for a specific command

cls: clears the command line

Network troubleshooting:

ipconfig : The terminal output below shows our IP address, subnet mask, and default gateway.

ipconfig /all : Adds extra info for example DHCP is enabled or not

tracert : Trace route, traces the network route traversed to reach the target.

nslookup: It looks up a host or domain and returns its IP address.

netstat : This command displays current network connections and listening ports. -a -b -o -n

File and Disk management:

cd: without parameters shows the current drive and directory

dir : lists the child directories /a displays hidden and system files, /s displays files in the current directory and all subdirectories.

mkdir : make directory

rmdir : delte directory

